@page "/components/chat"
@using Stil.Docs.Examples.Chat

<DocsHeader Title="Chat and comments" Eyebrow="Capture">
    <Lead>A conversation or a comment thread. Stil renders it; your app carries the messages.</Lead>
</DocsHeader>

<p>
    Both read your messages like the <a href="components/activity-log">activity log</a> reads its entries:
    <code>Time</code>, <code>Title</code> (the text), <code>Actor</code> (who wrote it), <code>Avatar</code> (a picture,
    or their initials) and <code>DetailsTemplate</code> for attachments or reactions. Sending raises <code>OnSend</code>
    with a <code>StilChatMessage</code> (the text and any files); add the message to <code>Items</code> and pass it on with
    SignalR or anything else. New messages from others are announced to screen readers. Both need an interactive
    render mode.
</p>

<h2 id="chat">Chat</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(Conversation)">
    <p>
        <code>StilChat</code> puts your own messages (<code>Mine</code>) on the other side in the primary color, joins
        messages one person sends within five minutes, and separates the days. The view stays at the newest message.
        Enter sends and Shift+Enter breaks the line (<code>SendOnEnter</code>). <code>Typing</code> lists who is typing,
        and <code>OnTyping</code> tells you, at most every three seconds, that the user is. <code>AllowAttachments</code>
        adds a button for files. The area is 28rem high; set <code>Height</code> to change it.
    </p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="comments">Comments</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(Thread)">
    <p>
        <code>StilComments</code> is the thread form, for a ticket, an inspection or an order: everyone on the same side,
        no bubbles, and a taller composer where Enter breaks the line and Ctrl+Enter (Cmd+Enter) posts.
    </p>
</DocExample>

